There's also the history.  Let's see if I can remember it correctly.

Long ago a blessed magic lamp was a guaranteed wish.  The DevTeam
decided that you shouldn't be able to wish for a wish because some
wishes (fountain, throne) are on-the-spot events that shouldn't be put
into the bank like that.  I'm not sure but I also think this was before
the current lighting and visibility system was written.  So a lamp was
a stored wish and so was wand of wishing and that's it.

Later came the vision system and the magic lamp had a second use,
so they added the 80/20 chance feature.  A blessed magic lamp
went from a guaranteed sotred wish to a guaranteed infnite light
source plus a likely stored wish.

Thus not wishing for a wish is a part of how it evolved across time and
it made perfect sense in an earlier version.



